WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:02.010
(wings flapping)

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:02.906
- Don't (beep) on me.

00:00:02.906 --> 00:00:06.763
(happy, upbeat whistling)

00:00:06.763 --> 00:00:07.881
- He's a keeper.

00:00:07.881 --> 00:00:10.475
- It was love at first sight
when I saw her, I knew.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:12.501
- There she was with her
chocolate brown eyes,

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.805
and looking cute and making
cute little squawking noises,

00:00:14.805 --> 00:00:16.500
and I got her.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.598
- We were walking by the kitty
cages, and all of a sudden,

00:00:19.598 --> 00:00:22.744
Melvin kind of reached his
little paw out and grabbed me.

00:00:22.744 --> 00:00:25.707
- Having these photos
would just be a memory

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:29.629
that I'll always have of how
happy I am when I'm with her.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.333
- And I've had her for 12 years,
longest relationship, yeah.

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:34.557
SO, this is an opportunity
forme to tell people,

00:00:34.557 --> 00:00:36.954
rescue a parrot if you want a parrot.

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:39.067
- [Becca] Melvin is a kitten,
he's only four months old,

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.340
so I think having him in
this age and me in my age

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.725
is like gonna capture the time

00:00:43.725 --> 00:00:44.970
when we kind of got to know each other.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:45.803
(camera clicking)

00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:48.140
- [Stu] In my spare time,
I'm a pro bono attorney

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.410
for a couple parrot
conservation organizations.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.603
As I've gotten to know more
about African Grey Parrots,

00:00:52.603 --> 00:00:55.722
I realized if one must have
one, they should rescue.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.932
But they're taken out of the
Congo by the the hundreds

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.603
in crates, most of them die,
so many people give them up.

00:01:00.603 --> 00:01:02.810
And once you have a parrot in your home,

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.827
for the most part, it's
too late for that parrot

00:01:04.827 --> 00:01:06.333
to ever be in the wild again.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:07.469
Yeah, I've kind of made it my mission to

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:09.324
get people to reconsider.

00:01:09.324 --> 00:01:11.436
If they don't have 900
square miles for a cage,

00:01:11.436 --> 00:01:13.642
then they probably shouldn't get a parrot,

00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:15.434
and if they must, definitely adopt.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:17.082
There are tons of them
out there that need homes,

00:01:17.082 --> 00:01:19.024
and they're super, super loving.

00:01:19.024 --> 00:01:20.798
- I had a 21 year old cat named Blossom

00:01:20.798 --> 00:01:22.270
who passed away in August.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.639
And, I never thought I would
ever get another cat again.

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:27.295
He is very hyper and
energetic, which is great,

00:01:27.295 --> 00:01:29.391
but it's kind of like a
baby where you have to watch

00:01:29.391 --> 00:01:31.292
him or he gets into stuff.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:32.608
All in all, it's an amazing experience.

00:01:32.608 --> 00:01:34.031
I have a little built in best friend.

00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:34.864
(camera clicking)

00:01:34.864 --> 00:01:37.297
- I heard this dog screaming outside.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:40.736
And, the gardeners had come
that day, I guess the gate

00:01:40.736 --> 00:01:42.673
got left open, I was
like, "Oh no, that's her."

00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:46.415
I ran outside, she had been hit by a car

00:01:46.415 --> 00:01:48.851
and this car had just kept going.

00:01:48.851 --> 00:01:52.115
When I ran up to her,
her tail started wagging,

00:01:52.115 --> 00:01:54.193
because she was just happy to see me.

00:01:54.193 --> 00:01:56.625
Her pelvis was just totally shattered,

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.025
and they told us that
we could either operate

00:01:59.025 --> 00:02:00.226
or put her down.

00:02:00.226 --> 00:02:02.901
What do you want, you want this?

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:06.839
In 2015, I was diagnosed
with a hip condition,

00:02:06.839 --> 00:02:10.372
like I woke up one day and I
just couldn't walk anymore.

00:02:10.372 --> 00:02:11.604
When I finally went in for surgery,

00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:12.833
I just kept thinking,

00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:15.649
Ella also had pelvic reconstruction.

00:02:15.649 --> 00:02:18.272
And if she can do it,
and she's this small,

00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:19.553
then I can do it too.

00:02:19.553 --> 00:02:20.914
Tell 'em who's boss.

00:02:20.914 --> 00:02:24.178
This dog is the love of my
life, like I cannot imagine

00:02:24.178 --> 00:02:26.770
what my life would be like without her.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:27.603
(camera clicking)

00:02:27.603 --> 00:02:30.386
- So, today is the unwrapping.

00:02:30.386 --> 00:02:32.990
- Never had pictures of Chiku
before done professionally.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:34.452
Just what my apartment needs.

00:02:34.452 --> 00:02:35.971
(paper crinkling)

00:02:35.971 --> 00:02:38.211
- Oh, you're a model.

00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:39.841
We can put this in your portfolio now.

00:02:39.841 --> 00:02:42.994
- Chiku. (laughing) It's great.

00:02:42.994 --> 00:02:43.827
(paper crinkling)

00:02:43.827 --> 00:02:47.106
- Oh my gosh, it's so beautiful.

00:02:47.106 --> 00:02:48.106
Oh, so cute.

00:02:49.442 --> 00:02:52.547
- This embodies us perfectly.

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:54.753
I think that these photos
showing us together,

00:02:54.753 --> 00:02:57.266
all healed up and so happy,

00:02:57.266 --> 00:02:59.766
and we're just two goofy gals.

00:03:01.394 --> 00:03:02.227
(laughing)

00:03:02.227 --> 00:03:04.038
- Best pals. (laughing)

00:03:04.038 --> 00:03:06.674
We're very handsome, I love
it, this is going on the wall.

00:03:06.674 --> 00:03:08.355
What do you think, hey Chiku.

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.258
(mouth popping) OK, I think she likes it.

00:03:10.258 --> 00:03:12.404
- I feel like we look
the same in this picture.

00:03:12.404 --> 00:03:15.890
Like our eyes are very
similar, and he's 100% my son.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.158
I never saw the resemblance before,

00:03:17.158 --> 00:03:19.718
but now, it's pretty clear,
like, this is my guy.

00:03:19.718 --> 00:03:22.627
- Yes, you should 100% get
a pet photo shoot done.

00:03:22.627 --> 00:03:24.692
I mean, you can take
pictures on your phone

00:03:24.692 --> 00:03:27.846
or take Instagram stories,
but having these printed out

00:03:27.846 --> 00:03:30.214
in high quality, this is
something I'm gonna have

00:03:30.214 --> 00:03:31.412
in my house forever.

00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:33.478
My kids are probably gonna
look at this one day.

00:03:33.478 --> 00:03:34.311
(camera clicking)

00:03:34.311 --> 00:03:36.404
- Um, I'll probably leave this to her

00:03:36.404 --> 00:03:39.075
so she can remember me when I'm dead.

00:03:39.075 --> 00:03:40.761
(whooshing)
(hinge squeaking)

